quran[27]{c,v,t}:
  89,24,He will say: ‘I wish I had sent ahead (some good) for my (real) life!’
  89,25,"On that Day, none shall be able to punish (anyone) like His punishment,"
  89,26,and none shall be able to bind (anyone) like His binding.
  89,27,(Allah will say to the righteous:) ‘O contented soul!
  89,28,"Return to your Lord, well-pleased (with Him) and well-pleasing (to Him)!"
  89,29,Then enter among My (chosen) servants!
  89,30,And enter My Paradise (the ultimate abode of My pleasure and nearness)!’
  90,1,"I swear by this city (of Mecca),"
  90,2,as you reside in this city* (O Esteemed Prophet!).
  90,3,"By the father and that whom he begot,*"
  90,4,"surely, We have created humankind in (a state of constant) toil and trial."
  90,5,Does he think that no one will have power over him?
  90,6,He says: ‘I have spent wealth in abundance.’
  90,7,Does he think no one has seen him?
  90,8,"Have We not given him two eyes,"
  90,9,"a tongue and two lips,"
  90,10,and shown him the two clear paths (of good and evil)?
  90,11,But he did not attempt the steep path (of goodness).
  90,12,What will make you realise what the steep path is?
  90,13,"(It is) the freeing of a slave,"
  90,14,"or feeding (someone) on a day of starvation,"
  90,15,"or (feeding) an orphan among relatives,"
  90,16,"or a needy (person) lying in the dust,"
  90,17,"and above all, being one of those who believe, urge one another to patience and urge one another to compassion."
  90,18,They are the people of the Right Hand.
  90,19,"But as for those who disbelieve in Our revelations, they are the people of the Left Hand."
  90,20,Upon them will be an enclosed Fire.
